-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">According to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means &lsquo;accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.&rsquo;However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion&rsquo;s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /><br /></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Yet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks&rsquo; Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p><strong style=\\\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\">&nbsp;</p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Q12. According to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, what the term &lsquo;banking&rsquo; refers to?</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"isComprehension\": false,\n          \"paragraph\": null,\n          \"paragraphText\": null,\n          \"fillUpsAnswers\": [],\n          \"nameText\": \"Directions (11-15): Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.\\n\\nAs the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman’s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers’ Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given underlying benefits/synergies.\\nTaking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.\\n\\nGiving a bank employee’s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.\\n \\nTill such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.\\nFor implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.\\n\\nThe humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.\\n \\nIrregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.\\nAccording to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means ‘accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.’However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion’s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.\\n\\nYet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks’ Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).\\n \\nThe IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.\\n \\nQ12. According to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, what the term ‘banking’ refers to?\",\n          \"sectionId\": \"60f69fb8e70c56aee9070d22\",\n          \"order\": 12,\n          \"questionSubmitOrder\": 12,\n          \"options\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The bank officers alone are responsible for executing the provisions of Sarfaesi Act.</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"The bank officers alone are responsible for executing the provisions of Sarfaesi Act.\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa6268651e1a\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Accepting money from public in order to lend and invest</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Accepting money from public in order to lend and invest\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa160a651e1b\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Repaying the money when demanded or withdrawn via cheque, order, draft and other methods</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Repaying the money when demanded or withdrawn via cheque, order, draft and other methods\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa707e651e1c\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Both (b) and (c)</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Both (b) and (c)\",\n              \"isCorrect\": true,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa383b651e1d\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">None of these</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"None of these\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa5c42651e1e\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"solution\": \"<p><strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: blue; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">Referring to the paragraph fifth, the provisions in the section 5 of banking regulation act are mentioned. Hence, option (d) is right answer choice.</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"hasMultipleAnswers\": false,\n          \"type\": \"multiple_choice\",\n          \"isAttempted\": false,\n          \"isPartiallyCorrect\": false,\n          \"isCorrect\": false,\n          \"isGraceMarked\": false,\n          \"isReevaluated\": false,\n          \"isBookmark\": false,\n          \"studentQuestionId\": \"6ab02797e59d370af93ba724\",\n          \"marks\": {\n            \"positive\": 0,\n            \"negative\": 0\n          },\n          \"timeTaken\": 0,\n          \"markForReview\": false,\n          \"isGpscType\": false,\n          \"isSurrendered\": false,\n          \"difficultyLevel\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"_id\": \"60f69fd0104d43b4d976b0e8\",\n          \"name\": \"<p>&nbsp;</p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Directions (11-15):&nbsp;Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /></span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">As the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman&rsquo;s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers&rsquo; Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given&nbsp;underlying benefits/synergies.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Taking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /><br /></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Giving a bank employee&rsquo;s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Till such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">For implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /></span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Irregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">According to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means &lsquo;accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.&rsquo;However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion&rsquo;s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /><br /></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Yet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks&rsquo; Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.</span></strong></p>\\n<p style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);\\\">&nbsp;</p>\\n<p style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);\\\">&nbsp;<strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem; color: #333333;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Q13. What causes traumatisation of bank employees according to the passage given above?</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\">&nbsp;</p>\\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\",\n          \"isComprehension\": false,\n          \"paragraph\": null,\n          \"paragraphText\": null,\n          \"fillUpsAnswers\": [],\n          \"nameText\": \" \\nDirections (11-15): Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.\\n\\nAs the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman’s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers’ Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given underlying benefits/synergies.\\nTaking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.\\n\\nGiving a bank employee’s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.\\n \\nTill such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.\\nFor implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.\\n\\nThe humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.\\n \\nIrregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.\\nAccording to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means ‘accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.’However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion’s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.\\n\\nYet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks’ Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).\\n \\nThe IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.\\n \\n Q13. What causes traumatisation of bank employees according to the passage given above?\\n \\n \",\n          \"sectionId\": \"60f69fb8e70c56aee9070d22\",\n          \"order\": 13,\n          \"questionSubmitOrder\": 13,\n          \"options\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Bank officers are targeted personally for implementation of Sarfaesi Act</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Bank officers are targeted personally for implementation of Sarfaesi Act\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa0fa6651ded\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Sometimes the retirement benefits are withheld</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Sometimes the retirement benefits are withheld\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa02d7651dee\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Irregular working hours, stress due to financial risk, technical and IT issues</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Irregular working hours, stress due to financial risk, technical and IT issues\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa10e4651def\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">All of the above</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"All of the above\",\n              \"isCorrect\": true,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa2327651df0\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">None of these</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"None of these\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa7a90651df1\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"solution\": \"<p><strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: blue; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">Paragraph third and fourth of this passage contains the reasons behind the traumatisation of bank employees. So, option (d) is correct answer choice.</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"hasMultipleAnswers\": false,\n          \"type\": \"multiple_choice\",\n          \"isAttempted\": false,\n          \"isPartiallyCorrect\": false,\n          \"isCorrect\": false,\n          \"isGraceMarked\": false,\n          \"isReevaluated\": false,\n          \"isBookmark\": false,\n          \"studentQuestionId\": \"6ab02797e59d3700c83ba725\",\n          \"marks\": {\n            \"positive\": 0,\n            \"negative\": 0\n          },\n          \"timeTaken\": 0,\n          \"markForReview\": false,\n          \"isGpscType\": false,\n          \"isSurrendered\": false,\n          \"difficultyLevel\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"_id\": \"60f69fd0104d43224b76b0ed\",\n          \"name\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Directions (11-15):&nbsp;Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><!-- [if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br /><!--[endif]--></span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">As the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman&rsquo;s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers&rsquo; Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given&nbsp;underlying benefits/synergies.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Taking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\"><br /><br /><!-- [if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br /><!--[endif]--></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Giving a bank employee&rsquo;s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Till such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">For implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><!-- [if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br /><!--[endif]--></span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Irregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">According to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means &lsquo;accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.&rsquo;However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion&rsquo;s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\"><br /><br /><!-- [if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br /><!--[endif]--></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Yet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks&rsquo; Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p><strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\">&nbsp;</p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Q14. According to the above passage, what could be the other factors apart from profitability for revising wages of bankers?</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"isComprehension\": false,\n          \"paragraph\": null,\n          \"paragraphText\": null,\n          \"fillUpsAnswers\": [],\n          \"nameText\": \"Directions (11-15): Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.\\n\\nAs the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman’s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers’ Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given underlying benefits/synergies.\\nTaking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.\\n\\nGiving a bank employee’s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.\\n \\nTill such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.\\nFor implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.\\n\\nThe humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.\\n \\nIrregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.\\nAccording to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means ‘accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.’However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion’s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.\\n\\nYet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks’ Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).\\n \\nThe IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.\\n \\nQ14. According to the above passage, what could be the other factors apart from profitability for revising wages of bankers?\",\n          \"sectionId\": \"60f69fb8e70c56aee9070d22\",\n          \"order\": 14,\n          \"questionSubmitOrder\": 14,\n          \"options\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Bank employees spend a huge amount of working hours in the sale of para-banking products and implementing government schemes though it is not mentioned in the section 5 of banking regulation act.</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Bank employees spend a huge amount of working hours in the sale of para-banking products and implementing government schemes though it is not mentioned in the section 5 of banking regulation act.\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aad7f8651dfc\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">While the balance sheet becomes red due to NPAs, they are blamed for non-performance and profitability</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"While the balance sheet becomes red due to NPAs, they are blamed for non-performance and profitability\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa6698651dfd\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Instead of making essential amendments to SARFAESI Act that shows lack of political fraternity, bank officers are forced to implement its provisions</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Instead of making essential amendments to SARFAESI Act that shows lack of political fraternity, bank officers are forced to implement its provisions\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa6c54651dfe\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Their retirement benefits are withdrawn in many cases and many of them get arrested without having awareness of the reason behind the arrest even resulting into suicides</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Their retirement benefits are withdrawn in many cases and many of them get arrested without having awareness of the reason behind the arrest even resulting into suicides\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aae8d1651dff\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">All of the above</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"All of the above\",\n              \"isCorrect\": true,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa461b651e00\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"solution\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: blue; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">As mentioned in paragraph 5th, we can conclude that all these acts of bankers should be considered for wage revision. Since, all the points are supporting according to the facts given in the passage, so option (e) is right answer choice.</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"hasMultipleAnswers\": false,\n          \"type\": \"multiple_choice\",\n          \"isAttempted\": false,\n          \"isPartiallyCorrect\": false,\n          \"isCorrect\": false,\n          \"isGraceMarked\": false,\n          \"isReevaluated\": false,\n          \"isBookmark\": false,\n          \"studentQuestionId\": \"6ab02797e59d374ad63ba726\",\n          \"marks\": {\n            \"positive\": 0,\n            \"negative\": 0\n          },\n          \"timeTaken\": 0,\n          \"markForReview\": false,\n          \"isGpscType\": false,\n          \"isSurrendered\": false,\n          \"difficultyLevel\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"_id\": \"60f69fd0104d4318e476b0f2\",\n          \"name\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Directions (11-15):&nbsp;Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /></span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">As the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman&rsquo;s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers&rsquo; Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given&nbsp;underlying benefits/synergies.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Taking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /><br /></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Giving a bank employee&rsquo;s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Till such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">For implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /></span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Irregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">According to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means &lsquo;accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.&rsquo;However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion&rsquo;s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /></span></strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"><br /><br /><br /></span></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><strong><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Yet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks&rsquo; Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).</span></strong></p>\\n<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65); text-align: justify; line-height: 21.75pt; background: #f9f9f9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">&nbsp;</span></p>\\n<p style=\\\"margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);\\\"><strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.</span></strong></p>\\n<p><strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Q15. According to Jyothi KP, how government should help banks in realizing the public money?</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"isComprehension\": false,\n          \"paragraph\": null,\n          \"paragraphText\": null,\n          \"fillUpsAnswers\": [],\n          \"nameText\": \"Directions (11-15): Read the following passage and answer the following questions based on the given passage.\\n\\nAs the country celebrates 50 years since bank nationalisation, bank employees will be proud that they have contributed to nation-building. Still there are basic issues close to the bankman’s heart that are yet to find redressal, observes Jyothi KP, Vice-President, All-India Bank Officers’ Confederation, Kerala, and a National Executive Committee member.The Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Acts of 1970 and 1980 provide that the Central Government, in consultation with the Reserve Bank of India, may make a scheme, inter alia, for amalgamation of any nationalised bank with any other nationalised bank or any other banking institution. Various committees, including Narasimhan Committee (1998) constituted by the RBI, Leeladhar Committee (2008) chaired by the RBI Deputy Governor, and the Nayak Committee (2014) constituted by the RBI, have recommended consolidation of public sector banks (PSBs) given underlying benefits/synergies.\\nTaking note of this and potential benefits of consolidation for banks as well as the public through enhanced access to banking services, the government, in order to facilitate consolidation among PSBs to create strong and competitive banks, serving as catalysts for growth, with improved risk profile, has approved a framework for proposals to amalgamate PSBs through an Alternative Mechanism.The following amalgamation/mergers have already happened post-nationalisation and some more are reportedly in the pipeline. This creates stress for the employees since they are scared for their existence and job security, observes Jyothi.\\n\\nGiving a bank employee’s perspective, Jyothi recalled that the banking sector was in the red in Q4 of 2018-19 with a loss of ₹20,817 crore. In 2017-18, they had reported a massive loss of ₹85,000 crore forcing lenders to make provisions for bad loans and clean-up of the books.\\n \\nTill such time a project is commissioned in line with the approved schedule, banks should not be forced to categorise such projects as NPA, notes Jyothi. In the event of classification of big-ticket advances as NPA, the government should pro-actively help banks in realising the public money. It should initiate steps to declare suo moto 50 top NPAs of each banks as wilful defaulters and to publish their names and photos.\\nFor implementing SARFAESI provisions, many bank officers are targeted, even personally. By merely targeting the bank officers responsible for executing the Act, the political fraternity is missing the point to bring amendments to the Act itself.\\n\\nThe humongous challenge of realising the NPA is telling on PSB bottomlines. This is also subjecting the desk officers to unreasonable amount of work pressure and stress.\\n \\nIrregular working hours, stress on account of financial risk in routine work schedules, technical problems of software, and IT-related issues add to the worries of the already traumatised bank employees.In many cases, their retirement benefits are withheld. Many are arrested and are not aware as to why the arrest is happening in the first place, evening leading to suicides.\\nAccording to Section 5 of the Banking Regulation Act, banking means ‘accepting, for the purpose of lending and investment of deposits of money from public, repayable on demand or otherwise and withdrawal by cheque, draft, order or otherwise.’However, sale of para-banking products and implementation of government schemes take away the lion’s share of working hours of an average PSB employee.As mentioned earlier, when the balance sheet turns red, all blame is shoved on the desk-level officers for non-profitability/non- performance.\\n\\nYet, when it comes to wage revision, the question of profitability arise. The settlement takes place between Indian Banks’ Association (IBA) and United Forum of Bank Unions (UFBU).\\n \\nThe IBA represents bank managements and the UFBU, officers, employees, and staff organisations. The Charter of demands had been submitted in a time bound manner and the IBA had agreed to complete the process of negotiations expeditiously within the time-frame so as to reach the settlement before October 2017. However, since five major bank managements have not given full mandate for negotiating wages up to scale VII , the AIBOC is not participating in the talks now.\\nQ15. According to Jyothi KP, how government should help banks in realizing the public money?\",\n          \"sectionId\": \"60f69fb8e70c56aee9070d22\",\n          \"order\": 15,\n          \"questionSubmitOrder\": 15,\n          \"options\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Banks should not be forced to categorize bad loans as NPAs till a project through an alternative mechanism is not commissioned.</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Banks should not be forced to categorize bad loans as NPAs till a project through an alternative mechanism is not commissioned.\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa22d1651e0b\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The government initiate steps for declaring suo moto in which 50 Top Non Performing Assets of each banks are identified</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"The government initiate steps for declaring suo moto in which 50 Top Non Performing Assets of each banks are identified\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa16b7651e0c\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">The information of such NPAs should be published publicly as wilful defaulters alongside their names and photos</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"The information of such NPAs should be published publicly as wilful defaulters alongside their names and photos\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa1c81651e0d\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background: #F9F9F9;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">Both (b) and (c)</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"Both (b) and (c)\",\n              \"isCorrect\": true,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa694e651e0e\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"<p><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\">None of these</span></p>\",\n              \"nameText\": \"None of these\",\n              \"isCorrect\": false,\n              \"_id\": \"60f6b26d3be0aa1068651e0f\",\n              \"isMarked\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"solution\": \"<p><strong style=\\\"text-align: justify; font-size: 1.4rem;\\\"><span lang=\\\"EN-IN\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Arial','sans-serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: blue; mso-fareast-language: EN-IN;\\\">Here, In the third paragraph of the passage, KP Jyothi is stating the measures how government should help banks in realising public money by initiating suo moto. Therefore, option (d) is correct answer selection.</span></strong></p>\",\n          \"hasMultipleAnswers\": false,\n          \"type\": \"multiple_choice\",\n          \"isAttempted\": false,\n          \"isPartiallyCorrect\": false,\n          \"isCorrect\": false,\n          \"isGraceMarked\": false,\n          \"isReevaluated\": false,\n          \"isBookmark\": false,\n          \"studentQuestionId\": \"6ab02797e59d3709b13ba727\",\n          \"marks\": {\n            \"positive\": 0,\n            \"negative\": 0\n          },\n          \"timeTaken\": 0,\n          \"markForReview\": false,\n          \"isGpscType\": false,\n          \"isSurrendered\": false,\n          \"difficultyLevel\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"numberOfQuestions\": 15\n    }\n  ],\n  \"userDetails\": {\n    \"name\": \"HackWithInfyPrep\",\n    \"userId\": 192606116,\n    \"orgId\": 44032\n  },\n  \"sts\": 1789929704600,\n  \"region\": {\n    \"timeFormat\": \"hh:mm a\",\n    \"dateTimeStamp\": \"yyyy/MM/dd\"\n  }\n}"